    "code_caution": "Three 2026 ordinances (Ord. No. 26-01, 26-02 and 26-03) are listed as New Laws with no subject or chapter shown. They were not read (PDF only) and may amend the zoning chapter.",
    "checks": [
      "The zoning code has no accessory dwelling unit, accessory apartment, in-law, ECHO or similar rule. The single-family zones permit single-family detached dwellings and 'Accessory uses customarily incidental to the above permitted uses' (150-14, 150-24, 150-33, 150-42, 150-51, 150-69, 150-75)",
      "'Unless otherwise specifically provided in other provisions of this chapter, only one specific principal use shall be allowed on a lot of land' (150-12.1). A dwelling unit is occupied by 'not more than one family and having separate cooking and sanitary facilities' (150-5)",
      "A use not specifically allowed may be allowed by special exception where similar uses are permitted (150-9). A second dwelling may instead be read as a two-family dwelling, which the single-family zones do not list. Ask the Zoning Officer",
      "Two-family conversion of a detached single-family dwelling is a special exception only in the Local Commercial (LC) Zone: lot 8,000 sq ft, public sewer and water, no outside change except fire escapes (150-85D, 150-354)",
      "Duplex dwellings are permitted in R-4 (7,260 sq ft per unit) and R-6 (4,000 sq ft lot), and in the MU Zone and the Planned Residential Development Overlay (150-60, 150-63, 150-75, 150-78, 150-116.2, 150-228.21)",
      "No accessory use (except permitted signs) in the front yard, the area between the street line and the house, in A, R, R-1, R-2, R-3 and R-6. Accessory buildings 15 ft high (20 ft in R-1 and R-2) (150-20D, 150-29B, 150-30B, 150-38B, 150-39B, 150-47B, 150-48B, 150-56B, 150-57B, 150-73, 150-80)",
      "Every dwelling unit at least 700 sq ft of habitable floor area for a single-family, duplex or townhouse unit, 350 sq ft for a one-person efficiency (150-235)"
    ],
